{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To instruct the TestContext framework to load a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " instead of a standard "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", you can annotate the respective test class with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@WebAppConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The presence of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@WebAppConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " on your test class instructs the TestContext framework (TCF) that a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " (WAC) should be loaded for your integration tests. In the background, the TCF makes sure that a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MockServletContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is created and supplied to your test’s WAC. By default, the base resource path for your "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MockServletContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is set to "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "src/main/webapp"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". This is interpreted as a path relative to the root of your JVM (normally the path to your project). If you are familiar with the directory structure of a web application in a Maven project, you know that "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "src/main/webapp"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is the default location for the root of your WAR. If you need to override this default, you can provide an alternate path to the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@WebAppConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation (for example, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@WebAppConfiguration(\"src/test/webapp\")"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "). If you wish to reference a base resource path from the classpath instead of the file system, you can use Spring’s "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "classpath:"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " prefix."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Note that Spring’s testing support for "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " implementations is on par with its support for standard "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " implementations. When testing with a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", you are free to declare XML configuration files, Groovy scripts, or "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " classes by using "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". You are also free to use any other test annotations, such as "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ActiveProfiles"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@TestExecutionListeners"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Sql"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Rollback"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", and others."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The remaining examples in this section show some of the various configuration options for loading a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". The following example shows the TestContext framework’s support for convention over configuration:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension.class)\n\n// defaults to \"file:src/main/webapp\"\n@WebAppConfiguration\n\n// detects \"WacTests-context.xml\" in the same package\n// or static nested @Configuration classes\n@ContextConfiguration\nclass WacTests {\n\t//...\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension::class)\n\n// defaults to \"file:src/main/webapp\"\n@WebAppConfiguration\n\n// detects \"WacTests-context.xml\" in the same package\n// or static nested @Configuration classes\n@ContextConfiguration\nclass WacTests {\n\t//...\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Conventions"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "If you annotate a test class with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@WebAppConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " without specifying a resource base path, the resource path effectively defaults to "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "file:src/main/webapp"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". Similarly, if you declare "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " without specifying resource "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "locations"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", component "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "classes"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", or context "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "initializers"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", Spring tries to detect the presence of your configuration by using conventions (that is, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WacTests-context.xml"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " in the same package as the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WacTests"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " class or static nested "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " classes)."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The following example shows how to explicitly declare a resource base path with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@WebAppConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and an XML resource location with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ":"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension.class)\n\n// file system resource\n@WebAppConfiguration(\"webapp\")\n\n// classpath resource\n@ContextConfiguration(\"/spring/test-servlet-config.xml\")\nclass WacTests {\n\t//...\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension::class)\n\n// file system resource\n@WebAppConfiguration(\"webapp\")\n\n// classpath resource\n@ContextConfiguration(\"/spring/test-servlet-config.xml\")\nclass WacTests {\n\t//...\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Default resource semantics"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The important thing to note here is the different semantics for paths with these two annotations. By default, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@WebAppConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " resource paths are file system based, whereas "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " resource locations are classpath based."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The following example shows that we can override the default resource semantics for both annotations by specifying a Spring resource prefix:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension.class)\n\n// classpath resource\n@WebAppConfiguration(\"classpath:test-web-resources\")\n\n// file system resource\n@ContextConfiguration(\"file:src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/servlet-config.xml\")\nclass WacTests {\n\t//...\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension::class)\n\n// classpath resource\n@WebAppConfiguration(\"classpath:test-web-resources\")\n\n// file system resource\n@ContextConfiguration(\"file:src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/servlet-config.xml\")\nclass WacTests {\n\t//...\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Explicit resource semantics"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Contrast the comments in this example with the previous example."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Loading a "
      },
      {
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "WebApplicationContext"
          }
        ],
        "kind": "monospace",
        "roles": []
      }
    ]
  }
